import definition         stdlib/divisibility/odd

theorem odd-difference-of-squares
  note        An odd number is 2k + 1, and (k + 1)² − k² = 2k + 1.
  let n ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  assume n is odd                                                     (H2)
  then there exist a, b ∈ ℤ such that n = a² − b²

1.  k ∈ ℤ. n = 2k + 1.
    obtain k: def:odd, from H2

2.  n = (k + 1)² − k²
    calculation
      n = 2k + 1               1
        = (k + 1)² − k²        algebra

3.  There exist a, b ∈ ℤ such that n = a² − b².
    exhibit, from 2
